// PARAM: --analysis congruence --context call-string --context-depth 2 --dot
// Call-string GraphViz coverage at Congruence, the sibling of
// 05-callstring_graph_sign.vimp and 06-callstring_graph_int.vimp.
//
// This pins a crash, not a precision claim. cs_ctx_domain_for and
// cs_ctx_check_annotation (State_Report_Graph.thy) enumerated their
// analysis_domain cases and omitted Congruence_Analysis. Isabelle fills a
// missing case with undefined without complaining, the serializer emits a
// non-exhaustive OCaml match, and every renderer on this route died with
// "Pattern matching failed" while valid_analysis_config accepted the
// combination and the text report answered normally. --dot is the flag
// that reaches those two constants; run.py fails the case on a non-zero
// exit, which is exactly what the defect produced.
//
// The program is a witness the route can actually decide, so the case
// stays meaningful once it renders: mid is entered under two distinct call
// strings, and each carries its own singleton through dbl, so combine
// reads back 12 and 18 exactly. Context-insensitively both are UNKNOWN at
// 0 (mod 3) -- the two call sites join to 3 (mod 3) at mid's entry.
fun dbl(p) { return p + p; }
fun mid(p) { t = dbl(p); return t; }
fun main() {
  x = mid(6);
  y = mid(9);
  __voblint_check(x == 12); // PROVED
  __voblint_check(y == 18); // PROVED
}
